items.omniroute_state:
20128: there is no bounded rule. The OAuth occupancy override is an unbounded break: any OAuth peer with strictly fewer foreign in-flight sessions and priority <= pinned+1 replaces the pin (omniroute@dd6e9607e:src/sse/services/auth.ts:2159-2177; availability 1/(1+foreign sessions), open-sse/services/oauthSessionOccupancy.ts:19-41). Eligibility breaks clear the pin (sessionAffinityPin.ts:299; filters at :486-511).
Measured (route-mapper-final.json):
- occupancy explains 334/460 overrides, against 166/4001 kept turns where a less-occupied eligible peer existed;
- per-thread switch rate 4.73% (248 switches in 5246 turn pairs; the previous turn returned 200 in 244 of 248);
- cache-read share 53.93% after a switch vs 93.55% on the same account;
- switch-based estimate: 7,520,091 uncached input tokens per 24 h. It overlaps P1's served≠pin estimate and must not be added to it.
20129: not applicable (single connection).

